{"name":"Below the Surface","hex":"#0a2f7c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"below the surface","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Prepositional phrase","definitions":["Synonym of beneath the surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/below_the_surface"}],"entries":[{"title":"Below the Surface (1938 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Below the Surface is a 1938 adventure film set in the coal region of Newcastle, Australia. Only part of the movie survives."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Below_the_Surface_(1938_film)","wikidata":"Q12102124"},{"title":"Below the Surface (1920 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Below the Surface is a surviving 1920 American silent drama film directed by Irvin Willat and starring Hobart Bosworth. Thomas H. Ince produced the picture with distribution through Paramount Pictures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Below_the_Surface_%281920%29_-_Ad_2.jpg/330px-Below_the_Surface_%281920%29_-_Ad_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Below_the_Surface_(1920_film)","wikidata":"Q3637867"},{"title":"Below the Surface (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Below the Surface is a Danish action hostage thriller drama television series, written and directed by Kasper Barfoed, that was based upon an idea of Adam Price and Søren Sveistrup. The first eight-part series focuses on an act of terrorism committed on the Copenhagen Metro, where fifteen people are taken hostage. Former soldier Philip Nørgaard, who is head of the PET Terror Task Force (TTF), tries to save the hostages with help from members of his elite team. TTF members are portrayed by Sara Hjort Ditlevsen, Alexandre Willaume, Flemming Enevold, Esben Dalgaard Andersen, Peder Thomas Pedersen and Kenneth M. Christensen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c4/BelowtheSurface.jpg/330px-BelowtheSurface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Below_the_Surface_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q29108232"},{"title":"Surface","blocks":[{"text":"A surface, as the term is most generally used, is the outermost or uppermost layer of a physical object. It is the portion or region of the object that can first be observed and with which other objects first interact."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Red_Apple.jpg/330px-Red_Apple.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surface","wikidata":"Q3783831"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/MJK34774_Gidseltagningen_%28Berlinale_2017%29.jpg/500px-MJK34774_Gidseltagningen_%28Berlinale_2017%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/MJK34774_Gidseltagningen_%28Berlinale_2017%29.jpg/1280px-MJK34774_Gidseltagningen_%28Berlinale_2017%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/MJK34774_Gidseltagningen_%28Berlinale_2017%29.jpg/500px-MJK34774_Gidseltagningen_%28Berlinale_2017%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The filming team of Below the Surface at the 67th Berlin International Film Festival","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMJK34774_Gidseltagningen_(Berlinale_2017).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Water_droplet_lying_on_a_damask.jpg/500px-Water_droplet_lying_on_a_damask.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Water_droplet_lying_on_a_damask.jpg/1280px-Water_droplet_lying_on_a_damask.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/